     "*   **Student RefNet ($\\Theta_s$):** 2-layer MLP, 64 hidden units.",
     "*   **Teacher RefNet ($\\Theta_t$):** 3-layer MLP, 128 hidden units.",
     "*   **Directional MLP:** 256 hidden units.",
     "*   For the first 5,000 iterations, only the base NeRF density $\\sigma$ is queried along the original ray.",
     "*   Convert the predicted 4D coordinates back to Cartesian direction $\\mathbf{d}_r$ and origin $\\mathbf{o}_r$.",
     "*   **Phase 1 (Stratified):** Sample along the original ray.",
     "*   Query density $\\sigma_i$ at points along the original ray using the Spatial MLP.",
     "*   Query density $\\sigma_{ir}$ at points along the refracted ray using the Spatial MLP.",
     "*   Apply importance sampling based on Phase 1 results to the original ray.",
     "**Refraction Loss ($\\mathcal{L}_{ref}$):** Ensures reversibility and physical consistency.",
     "*   **Time Complexity:** The method adds the cost of two additional MLP evaluations (Student and Teacher RefNet) and one Decoder MLP evaluation per ray per iteration."
